Doesn't look right to my reading of the source.  Here's how I read
dig.c:

Each turn of digging, you generate an amount of digging effort equal
to: 10-14 + to hit bonus/penalty for high str/dex + weapon enchantment
- erosion penalty for worst erosion + damage bonus for increase damage

(Note: yes, that's the to-hit bonus, not the damage bonus, for stats.
I don't know if this is a bug.  Other than that, it's pretty much the
formula for damage with a wielded weapon which does 10-14 damage per
hit)

(There's a special case for dwarves, after the effort is added to the
total effort, the *total* effort is doubled.  Each turn.  So they dig
a lot faster.)

It requires 50 effort to dig a pit.
It requires 250 effort to dig a hole.
Anything else requires 100 effort.  (statue, boulder, wall, stone,
tree, door, secret door)
Shop walls are handled specially, and I don't feel like digging
through that source right now, so this may not apply to them.

Things that make you dig faster:
* being a dwarf!
* wearing rings of increase damage
* having high dexterity
* having high strength
* enchanting your pick-axe
* removing erosion from your pick-axe

(Where applicable, the inverse of the above make you dig slower)

Things that do not make you dig faster:
* enhancing your skill at pick-axes
* luck
* using a dwarven mattock rather than a pick-axe


